  {
    "id": "mapnav",
    "title": "MapNav: A Novel Memory Representation via Annotated Semantic Maps for VLM-based Vision-and-Language Navigation",
    "authors": [
      "Lingfeng Zhang",
      "Xiaoshuai Hao",
      "Qinwen Xu",
      "Qiang Zhang",
      "Xinyao Zhang",
      "Pengwei Wang",
      "Jing Zhang",
      "Zhongyuan Wang",
      "Shanghang Zhang",
      "Renjing Xu"
    ],
    "year": 2025,
    "venue": "ACL 2025 long papers",
    "source": "https://aclanthology.org/2025.acl-long.638/",
    "pages": "1, 3–8",
    "problem": "Raw RGB-history accumulation costs memory and repeated visual encoding. MapNav substitutes an online annotated semantic top-down map for most history. Despite RGB-only-looking checkmarks in Table1, ASM construction explicitly consumes depth and pose (§3.2/Fig3), so the whole system is not a monocular RGB-only sensor baseline.",
    "method": "Construct M∈R^((n+4)×W×H): obstacle, explored, current-position, trajectory channels plus n semantic classes. Mask2Former segments RGB, depth gives point cloud, pose aligns successive observations, and projection updates BEV. Connected components over each semantic category above areaτ get centroid text labels, making a rendered ASM. Shared SigLIP-so400M encodes currentRGB andASM; spatial unpadding/patch merge Φ_spatial produces visual patches, separate2layerGELUprojectors map to Qwen2-7Bhidden space (Eqs1–3). LLaVA-OneVision generates text commands; regex Ψ(text,patterns) maps synonyms toForward/Left/Right/Stop (Eq4). No differentiability through mapping/regex is claimed by its 'end-to-end' policy terminology. Training approximately1Mtotalpairs, about300Koracle+200KDAgger+25Kcollision perR2R/RxR, with generalVQAco-training;8A100×30h. The500KR2R-only model is transferredzero-shot toRxR; thebest2historyframeversiontrainsbothR2R/RxR. Fulloptimization/lossmasksrequireappendix/code. At inference maintainASM,currentRGB and optionally2historyframes, thenparseactions.",
    "novelty": "Linguistically annotated map pixels align spatial memory with VLM OCR/semantic priors. Semantic maps, DAgger and collision recovery existed; novel map rendering and learned policy integration need separable controls. It is external mapping-plus-trainedVLM, not prompt-onlyMapGPT and notDUET.",
    "results": "Table1 RGB-onlywithinMapNav27.1SR/23.5SPL→ASM36.5/34.3R2R; adding2historyframes andRxRtraining39.7/37.2 andRxR32.6/27.7. This supportsASMwithinbackbone; changingtrainingdata limits attributing allbestmodelgain tohistory. Table4 semanticmap29.1SR vsASM36.5, but prose says originalmapimprovesbaseline although26.4<27.3. Table5 oracle23.9→DAgger33.5→collision36.5SR shows substantial datacontribution. Table3 .17MBconstantrepresentation vsNaVid276MBat300steps is storedobservationmemory, notfullmodel/GPUmemory; .25svs1.22s needs wholepipeline accounting. Real50instructionsfiveenvironments showsemanticadvantages but smallsamples.",
    "bottlenecks": [
      {
        "id": "MAPNAV-1",
        "description": "Mapping and text annotation can destroy appearance, height, temporal and relational detail",
        "conditions": "Repeated instances, depth/pose errors, map label clutter, long trajectories",
        "cause": "Fixed semantic categories and2Dprojection compress history; ASMraster/OCRmustresolveinstanceidentity",
        "evidence": "Fig3 sensorpipeline; Table1 adding2RGBhistoryframes helps; Fig5",
        "followups": "NavFoM/StreamVLNretainvisualhistory; PolarMemretrievescontext; no matchedmemorybudgetproof of sufficientmaprepresentation",
        "kind": "Methodological / insufficiently tested",
        "status": "Partially addressed; frontier remains uncertain",
        "confidence": "Moderate"
      }
    ],
