    "pages": "1, 3–8",
    "problem": "Existing VLMnavigation methods are tied to one camera layout/task/embodiment. NavFoM unifies indoorwheeled/quadruped,drones,vehicles andQA under boundedvisualtoken processing. It still needs task-specific action scaling/controllers and knowncameraazimuths.",
    "method": "DINOv2+SigLIP576patchfeatures concatenatechannels; gridpoollatestview to64patches,history to4,then2layerMLPtoQwen2-7B. TVI token E_base+P_time(TimePE(t))+P_angle(AnglePE(φ)) identifies timeandcameraangle; videoQAomitangle,imageQAomitboth. SinusoidalPEofsin/cosφpreservescircularidentity; sumsneednotprovablybeinjective overtimeandangle. BATS sampleshistorywithP(t)=(1−ε)exp(k(t−T)/T)+ε,ε=.1. Eq5 integralexpectedframes=(1−ε)(1−exp(−k))T/k+εT;Brentsolvekunder[(5E_frames)+65]N≤B_tokens. This is an expectation constraint, not a hard per-instance token cap; floorεmakesfeasibilityfailatsufficientlylargeT (authorsacknowledge1120stepsforfourcameras2048budget). Actionhiddenstate→3layerMLP predictsM=8waypointsinR4(x,y,z,yaw); taskscaleαrescalesthe[-1,1]coordinates; groundvehiclesignorez. L=10MSE(validwaypointdimensions)+QAautoregressiveCE. MSEmixespositionandyawunitsaftertasknormalization,so weightingdependsunits/scales. 12.7Mtotalexamples=8.02Mnavigation+3.15MimageQA+1.61MvideoQA;56H100×72h4032GPUh,oneepoch. 8Mnavigationincludes3.37MVLN,1.02Mobjectgoal,897Ktracking,681Kdrivingandwebvideos. SimulatorusestrajectoryactionsreplacingdiscreteForward/Left/Right;deployment19.1GB/218ms~5Hz1600tokensRTX4090.",
    "novelty": "Sharedcross-tasktrajectoryhead plus explicit time/camera-tokenorganization and budget-dependenthistorysampling, at muchlargerdatascale. ClosestUni-NaVidunifiesnavigationtasks withtokenmerging; NaVILAseparateshigh-levelnavigation/locomotion. Sampling-policyandcross-taskbenefitsrequirematcheddata/actionrepresentation.",
    "results": "Table1singleviewR2R56.2SR/51.2SPL,RxR57.4/49.4;fourview61.7/55.3and64.4/56.2. Table2unseenOVON43.6/31.3singleview;differentobjectgoaltrainsetsozero-shotasteriskdoesnotmeanuntrainednavigation. Table3tracking85.0SRvsTrackVLA85.1single-target,61.4vs57.6distracted. Table4NAVSIM84.3PDMSvsPARADrive84.0,UniAD83.4,LAW84.6. These broadresults supportgenerality, notsuperiorityeverymetric. Dataquantity andchangedactionspacearematerialconfounders.",
